ge and the fundamentals favor Democrats in this cycle's environment, but Iowa's six-point Republican lean, markets pricing Hinson ahead, and a late GOP super PAC surge argue for trimming the Democratic margin to near dead-even.", "watch": "Whether the GOP outside spending blitz and attacks on Turek's House voting record move late polls toward Hinson, or the national Democratic environment holds.", "confidence": "medium", "notes": ["Open seat: Joni Ernst (R) is not on the ballot."]}, "overview": "Iowa's Senate race is an open-seat contest after Joni Ernst's retirement, pitting Republican Ashley Hinson against Democrat Josh Turek, with a Libertarian also on the ballot. The state leans Republican by about six points, but the 2026 environment favors Democrats, and recent polls mostly show a razor-thin race. Averages put Turek up by roughly one to two points, though several Republican-leaning pollsters show Hinson slightly ahead, and one Marist survey showed a wider Turek lead.\n\nBoth sides are well funded: Hinson has raised over $10 million, while Turek has benefited from nearly $10 million in outside support, and a GOP super PAC recently added $20 million. Most expert raters call the race a tossup, with one tilting Republican and one leaning Democratic. Prediction markets currently give Hinson the better odds, reflecting the state's partisan lean. The race sits at dead even, with a slight Democratic edge on polling but real Republican upside.", "history": [{"date": "2026-09-22", "p_dem": 0.6012, "margin": 1.25}, {"date": "2026-09-23", "p_dem": 0.5782, "margin": 0.8}, {"date": "2026-09-24", "p_dem": 0.5857, "margin": 0.8}, {"date": "2026-09-25", "p_dem": 0.5846, "margin": 0.8}, {"date": "2026-09-26", "p_dem": 0.4983, "margin": 0.5}, {"date": "2026-09-27", "p_dem": 0.503, "margin": 0.5}, {"date": "2026-09-28", "p_dem": 0.579, "margin": 0.8}, {"date": "2026-09-29", "p_dem": 0.5896, "margin": 0.8}, {"date": "2026-09-30", "p_dem": 0.5557, "margin": 0.5}]}